*** Claude discovered bug: view-module-sort-mapping

set show advisories off .

*** The mapping of Bool, a sort declared in a module, is reported as not applied, and
*** then the view fails looking for true in the kind of B, as if it had been applied.
*** Expected: either the mapping ignored everywhere (and the view usable, since N has
*** true : -> Bool), or the mapping refused with a warning.

fth T is
  protecting BOOL .
  sort E .
endfth

fmod N is
  sort B .
endfm

view V from T to N is
  sort E to B .
  sort Bool to B .
endv

show view V .

*** We now check that refusing the mapping still allows the view to
*** re-evaluated if the from-theory changes.

fmod FOO is
  sort Foo .
endfm

fth T is
  protecting FOO .
  sort E .
endfth

fmod N is
  sort B .
endfm

view V from T to N is
  sort E to B .
  sort Foo to B .
endv

show view V .

fth T is
  sort Foo .
  sort E .
endfth

show view V .
